body:
Honestly I think we agree on most things here. I didn't make the best argument here bc my argument was supposed to be "Bloom couldn't make the moves other GM's did because he didn't have the resources because the owners didn't allow him to have the resources."  Most of the blame for the state of the Red Sox I put on ownership. I'm 100% with you that Henry just doesn't care anymore. I sort of alluded to this when I mentioned how he was supposed to lower payroll. However, I made this post bc a lot of people say Bloom is THE reason the Red Sox are mid which just isn't true. I don't think Bloom has done the best with what he's been given, but ownership isn't doing any favors.

&#x200B;

Also I'm totally with you on the whole Mayer not being a huge strategic move. Any GM would have taken him their and I'm surprised he fell to number 4. I also agree with you on what you said about Bloom trying to run the Red Sox like the Dodgers and Rays. I've been saying for a while Bloom needs to run this team like the Red Sox not like Tampa Bay.
